2. mechanical-dance — PHX-D01
   Copyright (c) 2026 jenghis / mechanical-dance.
   Source: https://github.com/mechanical-dance/PHX-D01
   The host-port design proven by PHX-D01 is reused here under GPL-3.0:
   - patches/01-oscillator-overflow-flag.patch is PHX-D01's patch, verbatim.
   - shim/ (stm32f7xx_hal.h, stm32f7xx.h, fatfs.h, usbd_cdc.h) is adapted from
     PHX-D01's shim, with __SADD16 and the __SMLALD family added (not called
     by the pinned firmware today; provided for the documented ARM DSP
     surface and covered by tests/test_intrinsics.c).
   - engine/ (engine.c, engine.h, kit.c, stubs.c) is adapted from PHX-D01's
     host/ wrapper: kit loading by front-panel CC replay, the parameter-127
     out-of-bounds skip, and the NULL-parameter-pointer scratch fix are
     PHX-D01's findings. PHX-D01's Eurorack-module mod matrix is not carried
     over (out of scope for this project).
   - tools/lxr-render.c is adapted from PHX-D01's host/render.c.
   - factory/INIT.SND is copied from PHX-D01's factory/ folder (the firmware's
     Initkit).
   - The Makefile's copy-vendor-then-patch build structure follows PHX-D01's.
